    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0514" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/693: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Chihuahua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Myers</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-15T19:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 12, 5 p.m. is being repeated to Embassy<anchor n="48" xml:id="d468-f1"
                    /> with instructions to request that appropriate Federal authorities in
                    Chihuahua be instructed by telegraph not to insist upon payment of taxes which
                    have already been paid by American citizens to persons exercising <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> authority in accordance with principles of
                    international law set forth in Department’s March 29, 4 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >6</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d468-f2"/> You will advise American
                    citizens who may be forced to repay such taxes to Federal authorities not to pay
                    except under protest and to demand receipts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d468-f1" n="48" xml:id="d468-f1-content">
